From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: World of Warcraft <warcraft@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:18:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Build: no DEBUG=1 for clang

Clang builds defined DEBUG for all of the core, GCC builds don't. With it, the Battle.net
server's code saw gSOAP's debug layout of struct soap (SOAP_DEBUG, SOAP_MEM_DEBUG: more fields)
while the gSOAP library was built without it, and gSOAP logs every message to files.
---
 cmake/compiler/clang/settings.cmake | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake/compiler/clang/settings.cmake b/cmake/compiler/clang/settings.cmake
index 3705f7a..a27071b 100644
--- a/cmake/compiler/clang/settings.cmake
+++ b/cmake/compiler/clang/settings.cmake
@@ -40,9 +40,9 @@ target_compile_options(trinity-compile-option-interface
     -Wno-narrowing
     -Wno-deprecated-register)
 
-target_compile_definitions(trinity-compile-option-interface
-  INTERFACE
-    -DDEBUG=1)
+# No -DDEBUG=1 (it was set here for every clang build): GCC's settings don't set it, and code that
+# includes gSOAP's header with it sees a different struct soap (SOAP_DEBUG, SOAP_MEM_DEBUG) from
+# the gSOAP library built without it.
 
 if (BUILD_SHARED_LIBS)
   # -fPIC is needed to allow static linking in shared libs.
